        <briefdescription>
<para>Checks the bisect limit to determine if the specified pass should run. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The method prints the name of the pass, its assigned bisect number, and whether or not the pass will be executed. It returns true if the pass should run, i.e. if the bisect limit is set to -1 or has not yet been exceeded.</para>
<para>Most passes should not call this routine directly. Instead, it is called through helper routines provided by the base classes of the pass. For instance, function passes should call <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_function_pass_1af9f5f511d75e16f09a5520cb9444cfa8" kindref="member">FunctionPass::skipFunction()</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
